        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lee Tamahori, Robert Redford, Greg MacGillivray, Pete Dexter, Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, John Malkovich\n- Films: Once Were Warriors, Die Another Day, Mulholland Falls, Grand Canyon Adventure: River at Risk\n- Topics: filmmaking, acting, directing, producing, narration, environmentalism, philanthropy\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Redford was born on August 18, 1936, and he is an American actor, director, producer, businessman, environmentalist, and philanthropist.\n- Lee Tamahori was born on 17 June 1950, and he is a New Zealand filmmaker.\n- Lee Tamahori is best known for directing the 1994 film Once Were Warriors and the 2002 James Bond film Die Another Day.\n- Mulholland Falls is a 1996 American neo-noir crime thriller film directed by Lee Tamahori and written by Pete Dexter.\n- Mulholland Falls stars Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, and John Malkovich.\n- Grand Canyon Adventure: River at Risk is a 2008 American documentary film directed by Greg MacGillivray and narrated by Robert Redford.",
